From 767c6c67effc1db4e13fd91601a8535701fae723 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:50:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Backport Abseil lifetime-capture attribute migration

Backport 0784689a65b4ea1329fbc5174b8a57c88ec796a9 to the selected
Abseil 20250814.1 source, adapting context while preserving all annotations.
Use lifetime_capture_by_this when supported and retain upstream's fallback
for older compilers. Migrate all this-owner uses in the seven affected
headers without suppressing deprecated-attribute diagnostics.

Declare the already-selected Abseil module as a direct dependency so the
included regression can compile public container, status, and mutex headers
and execute exclusive, shared, and writer RAII lock guards.

Base: rust-v0.162.1 (092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d)
with the downstream native warning policy and LLVM 23 prerequisite.
Red: bazel test //tools/build-warnings/abseil:lifetime_attribute_test
--keep_going rejects lifetime_capture_by(this) under -Werror.
Green: the same command, just fmt-check, and just bazel-lock-check pass.
Evidence: abseil-lifetime-red-with-direct-dependency.log,
abseil-lifetime-green.log, abseil-fmt-check.log, abseil-lock-check.log
in llvm-toolchain-Rkha0k.

Upstream: https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/commit/0784689a65b4ea1329fbc5174b8a57c88ec796a9
---
